WEBVTT

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.872
One pathway can oppose cancer in one tissue, and support it in another.

00:00:04.872 --> 00:00:07.785
That is the problem posed by SLIT2 and ROBO.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.545
SLIT2 is an extracellular protein.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:18.552
It interacts with ROBO receptors at cell surfaces, alongside other molecular partners.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:24.181
Blocking this interaction seems straightforward, until we ask which

00:00:24.181 --> 00:00:27.293
cells depend on it, and for what biological purpose.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.388
In some tumours, SLIT2 is silenced.

00:00:32.388 --> 00:00:38.283
Indiscriminate inhibition there risks suppressing signalling that may already protect tissue.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:45.220
In other settings, the pathway may contribute to invasion or immune exclusion.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.393
These contexts motivate research into inhibitors.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:53.508
Our review examined patent families from twenty twenty

00:00:53.508 --> 00:00:58.329
through twenty twenty-six, assessing their mechanism and experimental support.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.038
Antibodies can target ligands or receptors.

00:01:03.038 --> 00:01:08.775
Ligand traps offer another approach, with distinct manufacturing and evidence demands.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:14.296
Small molecules and macrocycles may disrupt protein contacts.

00:01:14.296 --> 00:01:18.286
But binding alone is not proof of a useful cellular effect.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:24.139
Nucleic-acid and bispecific strategies broaden the options.

00:01:24.139 --> 00:01:29.118
They still need evidence of specificity, exposure, and meaningful benefit.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:33.894
A patent is a proposed invention, not a clinical trial.

00:01:33.894 --> 00:01:38.092
A broad claim cannot substitute for working experimental data.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:45.359
Credible development requires biomarker selection, verified pathway direction,

00:01:45.359 --> 00:01:48.818
and tests in relevant models of each tumour context.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:53.909
Ultimately, the important question is when to intervene.

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:58.851
Inhibition needs biological justification, not merely a convenient target.
